Z||000000||burdell1||05-28-2000||03:03 PM||||What causes excessive blow back? Does blow back mean you are burning oil? My exhaust seems to be spitting out smoke, but it is white smoke (almost a grey.)||||reg||1
Z||000001||GT Bastard||05-28-2000||03:13 PM||||White smoke would be coolant more than likely.... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||05-28-2000||07:19 PM||||An educational short course in blow by is still available, but only in the blue smoke version.  Running rich in black smoke, and you just got home schooling in bad head gasket-white smoke.<P>Blown head gasket for white smoke in the exhaust is the best case senario, everything else is worse. Is the smoke still in the exhaust twenty minutes after startup?  Is it really in the exhaust or just following along from around?<P>Get a buddy and do the chase car thing, play with the gas and have fun.  Rock the Fiero under acceleration, your buddy can check for visible signs of exhilaration.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-28-2000||10:19 PM||||What about just a puff of white/gray smoke at start up, but nothing else no matter how hard I hit it?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||05-28-2000||11:18 PM||||Monkey, that's you valve seals.... I just fixed mine.  You'll need to pop your valves covers and dig into the heads.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-29-2000||02:06 AM||||Cost?  Difficulty?  What exactly is involved?  Will I still be able to run this for another 10k?  Will I blow it up if I get on it hard?||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||05-29-2000||06:41 AM||||do you get white smoke, or is it blue?<BR>If it is white smoke, it shouldn't do it all the time, and its just some water thats in your cylinders.<BR>If you get blue smoke every startup, your getting small amounts of oil seaping through the valve seals into the combustion engine.<P>You can run the car fine, you will know if it gets worse when its blowing smoke when your driving.  ||||reg||1
